 "text": "I've repaired the spec. All nine findings are fixed, and requirement IDs are unchanged wherever the meaning stayed the same.\n\n**One decision needs your confirmation: payments (REQ-75).** Your request (section 32) says the portal takes no online card payments in this phase. ASM-24 assumed Stripe card payments, but that came from a default setting and didn't answer its own question. I reconciled the two this way:\n- **This phase:** no payment-provider integration. Staff record the payment date manually, and the system records who entered it.\n- **Later:** if card payments are added, Stripe is the only provider.\n- **Card data:** the portal never stores it. A new check, AC-75.6, covers this.\n\nThis is flagged in the assumptions for you to confirm at review.\n\n**Removed (each pair contradicted itself):**\n- **REQ-85:** the sales report is now defined only by REQ-86. It counts all non-cancelled orders by order date, not only delivered ones.\n- **REQ-68:** the dashboard's failed-import count follows REQ-67 only, meaning failures since the last successful import.\n- **REQ-81:** only administrators create and edit customer companies. This matches the request, which gives Office Staff view and search only.\n- **NFR-2:** NFR-1 now sets one catalogue search target: 95% of responses within 1.0 s, with 50,000 products and 100 concurrent users. This meets the stricter of the old targets.\n\n**Changed:**\n- **One \"shall\" per sentence:** REQ-8, 21, 25, 38, 40, 54, 55 and 82 are reworded with the same meaning.\n- **Password reset (REQ-9, REQ-11):**\n  - No reset email goes to deactivated users, pending invitees or users of inactive companies, and the response looks the same as for any other request.\n  - Locked accounts can still reset.\n  - A reset link stops working if the user is deactivated or their company becomes inactive after it was sent.\n- **Order emails (REQ-47):** emails go to the Buyer who placed the order only while that Buyer is active and still belongs to the order's company. Otherwise, and for orders staff created, they go to the company's contact email.\n\n**Added:**\n- **REQ-87:** an administrator can't deactivate their own account or change their own role. Since only an active administrator can make these changes, this also means the last administrator can't be removed.\n\n**Not changed:** NFR-3/4, NFR-5/6/7, NFR-8/9 and NFR-15/16 still set conflicting targets for the same thing, the same problem as NFR-1/2. None of them were flagged, so I left them alone. They should be settled before testing starts.",
